  "rationale": "No single non-foothold step is a chokepoint, because the target has at least two independent routes. Route A: wifiGuest/internet -> iotDevice -> configSecret -> fileServer -> dbReplica -> crownData. Route B: exposedApi/wifiGuest/supplychain -> workstation or dmzWeb -> browserStore -> jumpHost -> shareMount, mailArchive or vaultRead (also dbReplica) -> crownData. Blocking iotDevice, configSecret or fileServer leaves route B open. Blocking browserStore, workstation, dmzWeb or jumpHost leaves route A open. Blocking any single collection step leaves another collection parent of the target reachable. Every other step lies on neither route, so blocking it changes nothing."
